Error fixtures for the embedded Ohm grammar. Each member has flag `o`,
so the archive needs no grammar member and no docker. Each .error member
is the output of `ohm-cli test match_error` on the .txt member of the
same test, and each .expected member the output of
`ohm-cli test match_error --expected`. Flag `N` removes the trailing
newline of the .txt member, so the input is as in error-reporting prd
section 3.

The text matches miniohm in the ohmjs/ohm:18.0.0-beta.15 docker image
(its runtime package.json says ohm-js 18.0.0-beta.13), run on a fresh
Grammar per input. One difference is by design: in emoji, miniohm counts
the column in UTF-16 units, so it reads col 14 and puts the caret one
column to the right. See error-reporting prd section 5.
-- star_x.txt --
G {
  S = *x
}
-- star_x.o.N.error --
Line 2, col 7:
  1 | G {
> 2 |   S = *x
            ^
  3 | }
Expected "}"
-- star_x.o.N.s.error --
Line 2, col 7: expected "}"
-- star_x.o.N.expected --
literal "}"
-- star_x.o.N.f.expected --
literal "|" (fluffy)
literal "~" (fluffy)
literal "&" (fluffy)
literal "#" (fluffy)
description an identifier (fluffy)
literal "\"" (fluffy)
literal "(" (fluffy)
literal "--" (fluffy)
literal "}"
-- unclosed.txt --
G {
  S = "a"
-- unclosed.o.error --
Line 3, col 1:
  2 |   S = "a"
> 3 | 
      ^
Expected "..", "*", "+", "?", "~", "&", "#", an identifier, "\"", "(", "--", "|", or "}"
-- unclosed.o.N.error --
Line 2, col 10:
  1 | G {
> 2 |   S = "a"
               ^
Expected "}"
-- unclosed.o.N.s.error --
Line 2, col 10: expected "}"
-- unclosed.o.N.expected --
literal "}"
-- trailing_h.txt --
G { S = "a" }
H
-- trailing_h.o.N.error --
Line 2, col 2:
  1 | G { S = "a" }
> 2 | H
       ^
Expected "{"
-- trailing_h.o.N.s.error --
Line 2, col 2: expected "{"
-- trailing_h.o.N.expected --
literal "{"
-- tab.txt --
G {
	S = *x
}
-- tab.o.error --
Line 2, col 6:
  1 | G {
> 2 | 	S = *x
           ^
  3 | }
Expected "}"
-- tab.o.s.error --
Line 2, col 6: expected "}"
-- emoji.txt --
G {
  S = "😀" | *x
}
-- emoji.o.error --
Line 2, col 13:
  1 | G {
> 2 |   S = "😀" | *x
                  ^
  3 | }
Expected "}"
-- emoji.o.s.error --
Line 2, col 13: expected "}"
-- line10.txt --
G {
  A = "a"
  B = "b"
  C = "c"
  D = "d"
  E = "e"
  F = "f"
  H = "h"
  I = "i"
  J = *x
  K = "k"
}
-- line10.o.error --
Line 10, col 7:
   9 |   I = "i"
> 10 |   J = *x
             ^
  11 |   K = "k"
Expected "}"
-- line10.o.s.error --
Line 10, col 7: expected "}"
